ary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/footprint#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4c93d7fe2dc3ca8c38","definition":"The audit trail left by a crashed program.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["carbon footprint","cyberfootprint","digital footprint","ecofootprint","ecological footprint","foodprint","footprinted","footprinting","footprints on the sands of time","noise footprint","plastic footprint","water footprint"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/footprint#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a025422687f09ff811","definition":"A trace left behind that gives evidence of some action having occurred.","example":"In a recent study with a movie recommendation site […], higher message interactivity in the form of footprints of user actions, responsive suggestions in a search box, and live-chatting with an online agent led to greater perceived contingency and engagement with the site, which ultimately created more positive attitudes toward it and higher intention to recommend the site to others.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["carbon footprint","cyberfootprint","digital footprint","ecofootprint","ecological footprint","foodprint","footprinted","footprinting","footprints on the sands of time","noise footprint","plastic footprint","water footprint"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/footprint#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f7ea284226d889773e","definition":"What a person has done before, as a profession or lifestyle, serving as a model for others.","example":"He is following in his father's footprints.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],